You are a unit test specialist. Analyze this {language} source file and identify ALL branches testable as PURE UNIT TESTS only.

A unit test: pure in-process, no I/O, no network, no file system, no database, no time source. Tests one method in isolation. All external dependencies must be absent or trivially injectable.

For each public method, output a JSON object with:
- "method": fully qualified name (ClassName.MethodName or function name)
- "signature": parameter list with types
- "branches": list of objects, each with:
  - "condition": what triggers this branch
  - "outcome": what happens
  - "test_scenario": one-line unit test description
  - "test_type_hint": "UNIT"

Focus ONLY on:
- Null/None/nil guard clauses with no external deps
- throw/raise/panic on invalid input (pure validation logic)
- switch/match/when cases on enum or primitive values
- Boundary comparisons on primitive values (< 0, == 0, > max, empty string/array)
- Format string construction paths (pure string logic)
- Early return conditions based on input shape only
- Pure computation branches (arithmetic, string ops, collection transforms)

SKIP branches that require DB, HTTP, file system, clock, or injected collaborators — those are int_mock or int_real.

Return ONLY a JSON array. No explanation, no markdown.

Source file ({language}):
```
{source}
```
